consecutive 600-unit buckets immediately after (2 in [22283,22882], 3 in [22883,23482]), consistent with a time-respecting relay under a 600-unit delay budget. Background activity on 749/632/1460 lies outside that burst, and the graph's hub (1566) is not on the path, so the finding is not explained by volume, popularity, or time-ignoring connectivity. Exact per-hop gaps were not directly observable, hence moderate confidence."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Structural funnel (unique candidate path).** In the window, 1885 has exactly one event: an out-edge to 749 (step_02, step_03, step_06). 749's only out-neighbour is 1453 (step_11); 1453's only out-neighbour is 1871 (step_12); 632's in-neighbours are 1184 and 1871 (step_13); 1460's in-neighbours are 632 and 765 (step_07), and 765 has no in-edges at all (step_14), so 765 cannot relay anything. The only possible influence route is therefore:\n\n**1885 \u2192 749 \u2192 1453 \u2192 1871 \u2192 632 \u2192 1460** (5 hops).\n\n**Temporal placement.** 1885's single event falls in [22283, 22582] (step_16). Bucketed counts over the chain's node set (step_15) show 2 events in [22283, 22882] and 3 events in [22883, 23482], then a gap \u2014 i.e. exactly five events on these nodes packed into ~1200 time units immediately following 1885's emission, matching the required 5-hop chain in order. The remaining events on 749/632/1460 (buckets at 21083, 23483+, 24683+, 26483+, 27083+) sit before 1885's event or long after the burst, so they are background traffic, not the relay.\n\n**Confounder controls.** Volume/popularity does not explain the link: the window has 2186 events over 1500 nodes with repeat ratio 0.004 (step_01), and 1885 (1 event) and 1460 (3 events) are both peripheral (step_02); the hub 1566 (60 events, step_08) is *not* on the path, so the connection is not an artefact of a high-degree broker. Static-connectivity alone was also insufficient \u2014 the 2-hop neighbourhood of 1885 (step_03) does not even reach 1460; only the directed 4\u20135 hop chain does.\n\n**Residual uncertainty.** Bucketed counts pin the events to adjacent 600-unit windows but do not prove every consecutive gap is \u2264600, so confidence is moderate rather than high.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_fdeac769\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1885, 749, 1453, 1871, 632, 1460],\n  \"window\": [18083, 27683],\n  \"confidence\": 0.62,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"A single directed chain 1885->749->1453->1871->632->1460 is the only route from source to target (all intermediate nodes have exactly one usable out/in edge; the alternative feeder 765 has no in-edges). 1885 emits once in [22283,22582], and precisely five events on the chain's nodes occur in the two consecutive 600-unit buckets immediately after (2 in [22283,22882], 3 in [22883,23482]), consistent with a time-respecting relay under a 600-unit delay budget. Background activity on 749/632/1460 lies outside that burst, and the graph's hub (1566) is not on the path, so the finding is not explained by volume, popularity, or time-ignoring connectivity. Exact per-hop gaps were not directly observable, hence moderate confidence.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 47592, "t